   "source": [
    "con.execute(\"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT 'bronze.sales_raw' AS stage, COUNT(*) AS row_count FROM bronze.sales_raw\n",
    "UNION ALL\n",
    "SELECT 'silver.step01_dedup', COUNT(*) FROM silver.step01_dedup\n",
    "UNION ALL\n",
    "SELECT 'silver.rejected_records', COUNT(*) FROM silver.rejected_records\n",
    "UNION ALL\n",
    "SELECT 'silver.cancelled_transactions', COUNT(*) FROM silver.cancelled_transactions\n",
    "UNION ALL\n",
    "SELECT 'silver.sales_clean', COUNT(*) FROM silver.sales_clean;\n",
    "\"\"\").df()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b74f7e95",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Cell 21 — Plot the funnel\n",
    "\n",
    "### Plot meaning\n",
    "This chart shows how many rows survive each major stage.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Business value\n",
    "It turns a complex cleaning pipeline into an easily explainable picture for stakeholders.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 46,
   "id": "72d45ef7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1000x400 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "df_funnel = con.execute(\"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT 'bronze.sales_raw' AS stage, COUNT(*) AS row_count FROM bronze.sales_raw\n",
    "UNION ALL\n",
    "SELECT 'silver.step01_dedup', COUNT(*) FROM silver.step01_dedup\n",
    "UNION ALL\n",
    "SELECT 'silver.rejected_records', COUNT(*) FROM silver.rejected_records\n",
    "UNION ALL\n",
    "SELECT 'silver.cancelled_transactions', COUNT(*) FROM silver.cancelled_transactions\n",
    "UNION ALL\n",
    "SELECT 'silver.sales_clean', COUNT(*) FROM silver.sales_clean;\n",
    "\"\"\").df()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10,4))\n",
    "plt.bar(df_funnel[\"stage\"], df_funnel[\"row_count\"])\n",
    "plt.title(\"Medallion Cleaning Funnel\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Stage\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Rows\")\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=25, ha=\"right\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "57725ce7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Plot interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "The funnel shows the cumulative effect of rule enforcement. If too many rows are lost, the upstream system may be unstable. If very few rows are lost, the source data is relatively healthy.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3230d9e7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Gold Layer\n",
    "\n",
    "Gold converts trusted Silver data into analytics-ready structures.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "11872613",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Cell 22 — Create Gold dimensions\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why\n",
    "Dimension tables store reusable business entities and descriptive attributes.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Business value\n",
    "They support slicing, grouping, and drill-down analytics.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 51,
   "id": "368e2d35-e988-4cf6-a5b8-c63a4ee6f935",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "<_duckdb.DuckDBPyConnection at 0x11073c730>"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 51,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "con.execute(\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE gold.dim_customer AS\n",
    "SELECT\n",
    "    ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY customer_email) AS customer_key,\n",
    "    customer_email,\n",
    "    -- =========================\n",
    "    -- CUSTOMER ATTRIBUTES\n",
    "    -- =========================\n",
    "    MIN(customer_name) AS customer_name,\n",
    "    MIN(customer_country) AS customer_country,\n",
    "    MIN(customer_city) AS customer_city,\n",
    "    MIN(customer_gender) AS customer_gender,\n",
    "    MIN(customer_segment) AS customer_segment\n",
    "FROM silver.sales_clean\n",
    "GROUP BY customer_email;\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
